A||||9||lowfunds||Engine dies when put in gear please help!!!!!!||||1||
Z||000000||lowfunds||04-11-2001||04:26 PM||||My engine dies on mt 87 auto when put into gear. It starts fine but When I put it in gear it instantly dies. Anyone have this happen. Need help stranded.||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||04-11-2001||04:30 PM||||I'll bet the TCC is stuck engaged. It's like starting the car with the clutch out. <P>Try disconnecting the TCC wires to the trans. You might luck out and it will disengage. You can at least drive it and get it fixed.<P>This is a common problem. The solenoid in the side cover gets dirt in it and sticks.<P>Terry||||reg||1
Z||000002||lowfunds||04-11-2001||05:30 PM||||terry more info where is the tcc located in my chilton it does not show it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||lowfunds||04-11-2001||05:34 PM||||bump<BR><p>[This message has been edited by lowfunds (edited 04-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Kerri 98||04-11-2001||06:06 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by lowfunds:<BR><B>bump<P><BR>[This message has been edited by lowfunds (edited 04-11-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>disconnect the plug facing forward on the transmission near the oxygen sensor<BR>||||reg||12
